{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361404,"nonce":"DukjQN77RQqkJV6d1wZ82bPPHcw=","title":"Awaited child state machines and async handler state machines are never freed","message":"The host frees a task's own state machine when its `ZyntaxPromise` drops (`PromiseInner::drop`, crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/promise.rs) and the 16-byte promise right after the entry call (`ZyntaxPromise::from_async_call`). An `await` on another async function calls that function's entry from inside the state machine: `lower_await_calls` (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/abi_emit.rs) keeps the child's promise in a slot, polls it, and on Ready clears the slot without freeing the child's promise or state machine. `__zyntax_effect_launch_handler` (crates/zyntax_embed/src/effect_runtime.rs) leaves an async handler's state machine and promise unfreed on purpose. A child completed through `resolve_future` also leaves its entry in `host_futures::SM_COMPLETIONS`, which nothing takes.\n\nDone: a parent releases a child's promise and state machine once the child is Ready and `sm_is_referenced` says no table names it; an async handler's are released when the handler completes; a test repeats nested awaits and async-handler performs without growth.","files":null}]}